_subagent` for automatic planning:\\n39: ```\\n40: dispatch_subagent(agent_type=\\\"CI-CD-Agent\\\", task_description=\\\"...\\\", \\n41:   dag_task_id=\\\"TASK-001\\\", auto_plan=true)\\n42: ```\\n43: \\n44: ### When auto_plan_enabled=false\\n45: Do NOT skip to DAG-exempt agent. ALWAYS dispatch @Meta-Planner first, then re-dispatch with planned dag_task_id.\\n46: \\n47: ## 4. Investigation-Task Pre-Dispatch Checklist\\n48: \\n49: Before dispatching any task containing investigation keywords (investigation, audit, diagnosis, debug, troubleshoot, root-cause, \\u8c03\\u67e5, \\u6392\\u67e5, \\u8c03\\u8bd5, \\u8bca\\u65ad, \\u6839\\u56e0):\\n50: \\n51: - [ ] Task description includes explicit instruction to search runtime logs\\n52: - [ ] Target agent has `read` permission to relevant log paths\\n53: - [ ] Log paths match agent's permission scope\\n54: - [ ] Task description mentions at least one concrete log path\\n55: \\n56: **Why**: Sub-agents default to code-only searches. Without explicit log instruction, investigation tasks produce incomplete conclusions.\\n57: \\n58: ## 5. Session Resume Protocol\\n59: \\n60: When deliverables are rejected, resume the original session instead of creating new one:\\n61: \\n62: ```\\n63: dispatch_subagent(\\n64:   agent_type: \\\"Coder-BE\\\",\\n65:   task_description: \\\"Fix deliverables: [rejection reason]\\\",\\n66:   dag_task_id: \\\"SAME-TASK-ID\\\",           // MUST be same as original\\n67:   resume_session_id: \\\"<session_id>\\\"       // From session_log DB\\n68: )\\n69: ```\\n70: \\n71: **Constraints**:\\n72: - Same dag_task_id as original dispatch\\n73: - session_log DB entry must exist\\n74: - Only valid for sessions in `armed` or `delivered` state\\n75: - Maximum 3 resume attempts per session\\n76: \\n77: ## 6. Do Not Re-Centralize on dispatch_subagent\\n78: \\n79: - For Scout/research help, use native `Task` directly.\\n80: - Do not require `subagent-preamble`.\\n81: - Do not add wrapper-only language to generic e